From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:43:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq807x: nwax10ax: drop the crypto engine

The DTS enables the crypto engine but not the BAM DMA controller it
uses, so the driver never probes and the kernel reports:

  platform 73a000.crypto: deferred probe pending: (reason unknown)

The stock firmware of these devices does not build the crypto engine
driver, and the CPU has the ARMv8 crypto extensions. Leave the crypto
engine disabled instead of enabling the BAM DMA controller.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
---
 .../files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq807x-nwax10ax.dtsi      | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq807x-nwax10ax.dtsi b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq807x-nwax10ax.dtsi
index f92d901bc8..a3c08fec9f 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq807x-nwax10ax.dtsi
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq807x-nwax10ax.dtsi
@@ -50,10 +50,6 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-&crypto {
-	status = "okay";
-};
-
 &edma {
 	status = "okay";
 };
